# football-trackers/.gitignore — the repo-wide safety net.
#
# ┌─ WHY THIS FILE IS LOAD-BEARING ─────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
# │ This project tracks CHILDREN. `roster.json` is the only place their real names   │
# │ live at rest; `auth-accounts.json` holds the coaches' argon2id password hashes;  │
# │ `ft.passwd` holds the broker credentials every wearable authenticates with.      │
# │                                                                                  │
# │ Git history is APPEND-ONLY. Once any of these is committed, `git rm` removes it  │
# │ from the working tree but NOT from history — recovery means rewriting every       │
# │ commit that followed. So this file has to be correct BEFORE the first `git add`,  │
# │ not after the first mistake.                                                      │
# └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
#
# The per-directory .gitignore files (server/ client/ vision/ firmware/) remain the local
# authority and are deliberately NOT folded in here — vision/.gitignore in particular is a
# scoped privacy firewall (ADR-0023 §3). A few patterns below duplicate them on purpose:
# duplication costs nothing in a .gitignore, and a rule that lives only in a subdirectory
# stops protecting the moment the same file is created one level up.
#
# Enforced by server/test/gitignore-guard.ts (`bun run test:gitignore`), which asserts both
# directions — sensitive paths ARE ignored, and required paths are NOT.

# ── Personal data & secrets: never commit ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Child names, per session. AUTH_ROSTER_FILE, default ./roster.json (server/roster-user.ts).
# The glob forms matter as much as the exact name: the realistic way this leaks is someone taking a
# copy before an edit — roster.json.bak, roster-2026.json, "roster copy.json" — every one of which
# holds the same twenty children's names as the original.
roster.json
*roster*.json
*roster*.json.*
# argon2id coach password hashes. AUTH_ACCOUNTS_FILE (server/auth-user.ts).
auth-accounts.json
*auth-accounts*.json*
# Per-session config incl. age band. SESSION_CONFIG_FILE (server/session-config.ts).
session-config.json
*session-config*.json*
# Session handover across a graceful restart (Phase 6). AUTH_SESSIONS_FILE (server/src/auth.ts).
# It holds sha256(token), never a usable bearer token — but it names every logged-in coach and its
# CSRF values, and it has no business in a diff.
auth-sessions.json
*auth-sessions*.json*
# VACUUM INTO backups of the telemetry store (server/backup-db.ts). Each one is a COMPLETE copy of
# children's raw location, so it is exactly as sensitive as telemetry.db — and the *.db rules below
# already catch the filenames the tool writes; this covers the directory wholesale, including any
# copy an operator drops in beside them.
backups/
/server/data/backups/
# mosquitto credential DB: `mosquitto_passwd -c ft.passwd ingest` (server/mosquitto/README.md).
# Upstream mosquitto/apache docs name this file half a dozen ways; cover the conventional ones.
# NOTE: ft.acl is intentionally NOT ignored — it maps pseudonymous player ids to topic scopes
# and carries no secret, so it stays reviewable in the diff.
*.passwd
passwd
pwfile
passwords
.htpasswd
# Anything env-shaped: ROBOFLOW_API_KEY (vision/docker-compose.yml), MQTT/AUTH overrides.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Local Claude Code permissions — machine-specific and may name local paths. Unanchored so a nested
# .claude/ (e.g. server/.claude/) is covered too; the root-anchored form was not.
settings.local.json
# Keys and keystores. Not used by the project today — which is exactly why there is no habit
# protecting them, and why the TLS edge (ADR-0009) will arrive without one.
id_rsa
id_dsa
id_ecdsa
id_ed25519
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore

# Host-compiled firmware test binary (firmware/test/host/ README command builds it in place)
/firmware/test/host/test_resilience

# ── Data at rest (telemetry is children's positions, timestamped) ────────────────────
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
# -journal: VACUUM against a backup (journal_mode=delete, which is what VACUUM INTO produces) writes
# a rollback journal holding the PRE-erasure page images of children's positions.
*.db-journal
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
# Backups and dumps carry exactly the same rows as the live store. `VACUUM INTO` backups
# (Phase 6) land as .db; a hand-rolled one is as likely to be gzipped or dumped to SQL.
*.db.bak
*.db.gz
*.db.bz2
*.db.xz
*.db.zst
*.sql
*.dump
# The containerised store's bind-mount target (Phase 2b).
/server/data/

# ── Footage & model weights, ANYWHERE ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# vision/.gitignore is the scoped privacy firewall (ADR-0023 §3) and stays the local authority —
# but it only protects vision/. A clip dropped in docs/ or at the repo root to "look at later" is
# the same children's faces with none of the protection. Capitalised extensions are listed because
# GoPro and iPhone write .MP4/.MOV by default, and Linux treats those as different files.
*.mp4
*.MP4
*.mov
*.MOV
*.m4v
*.mkv
*.avi
*.webm
*.360
*.insv
*.mts
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.engine
*.safetensors

# ── Dependencies & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
dist/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
# PlatformIO build tree + downloaded libdeps.
.pio/

# ── Test / report artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
test-results/
playwright-report/
playwright/.cache/

# ── OS & editor cruft ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# A vim swapfile holds the full plaintext of whatever is being edited — .roster.json.swp is the
# roster. All three suffixes: vim rotates .swp -> .swo -> .swn when several are open.
*.swp
*.swo
*.swn
*~
.idea/

# Site build artefacts (generated by site/build.py + mkdocs)
site/_build/
site/_vendor/
